        "policy_id": "POL-001",
        "section": "2. Account Monitoring",
        "summary": "Privileged account activity must be reviewed when unexpected access is detected. Unexpected access includes:\n\n- A successful login from an IP address that is neither on the account's registered known-IP list nor inside an approved network listed in POL-002.\n- Access to three or more distinct assets within 15 minutes from a non-approved source.\n- Privileged activity outside the account's normal working pattern (for example, weekend activity for an account that normally operates on weekdays).",
        "source_document_ids": [
          "POL-001"
        ]
      },
      {
        "policy_id": "POL-003",
        "section": "1. Least Privilege",
        "summary": "Accounts may access only the assets listed in their current, unexpired permission records. Access to an asset without a current permission record is unauthorized, even if the target system allowed the connection.",
        "source_document_ids": [
          "POL-003"
        ]
      },
      {
        "policy_id": "POL-003",
        "section": "3. Critical Assets",
        "summary": "Access attempts against **critical** assets (for example, production databases) by accounts without permission must be reported to the asset owner, whether or not the attempt succeeded.",
